From: Christopher Owen <root@your.mom>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 14:06:19 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Use native pitched DMA for large aligned FP32 logits

Upstream base: 4963739834a2a1c925e520b5727ca536b52016f6. Rationale: two isolated boots show pitched DMA 2.0 to 2.2 percent faster for 96 padded FP32 rows, with no compute launch. Revert the slower wide TileLang tile. Keep smaller copies, casts, unaligned and odd-column layouts in TileLang. Quality: exact owned payload copies, current device/stream, explicit CUDA errors; no fallback on failure. Tests: backend screening validates eager/captured outputs; added live-payload graph replay and a side-stream test; final integrated two-boot qualification pending. Upstream status: local experiment, not submitted.
